  "spans": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "WHY USE THIS?\n",
      "size": 20,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "FastAPI builds JSON APIs that web and mobile applications call over HTTP; type annotations help validate inputs and describe the API contract.\n\n",
      "size": 16,
      "color": "#212121"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "PURPOSE AND REAL-WORLD USE\n",
      "size": 20,
      "color": "#6A1B9A",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "A normal HTTP request ends with its response; a WebSocket keeps a connection open for two-way messages. A FastAPI endpoint accepts, reads, and replies. This is an echo server; a browser client uses the WebSocket API.\n\n",
      "size": 17,
      "color": "#212121"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "To run these examples locally, install ",
      "size": 16,
      "color": "#212121"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "pip install fastapi uvicorn httpx",
      "size": 16,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " plus any extra package named in the lesson. Save the server example as ",
      "size": 16,
      "color": "#212121"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "app.py",
      "size": 16,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " and start ",
      "size": 16,
      "color": "#212121"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "uvicorn app:app --reload",
      "size": 16,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": ". ",
      "size": 16,
      "color": "#212121"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "--reload",
      "size": 16,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " is for development only.\n\n",
      "size": 16,
      "color": "#212121"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "WHERE DOES THIS APPEAR IN REAL LIFE?\nA chat, shared board, or game room can push new events to a client immediately.\n\n",
      "size": 16,
      "color": "#212121"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "If this part is omitted: Polling repeatedly for updates adds delay and traffic; WebSocket uses an open connection.\n\n",
      "size": 16,
      "color": "#212121"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "COMPLETE RUNNABLE EXAMPLE\n",
      "size": 20,
      "color": "#1565C0",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "QUESTION: What will this code print? Predict first, then run it.\n",
      "size": 16,
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "python",
      "code": "from fastapi import FastAPI, WebSocket, WebSocketDisconnect\n\napp = FastAPI()\n\n@app.websocket(\"/ws\")\nasync def websocket_echo(websocket: WebSocket):\n    await websocket.accept()\n    try:\n        while True:\n            message = await websocket.receive_text()\n            await websocket.send_text(f\"Echo: {message}\")\n    except WebSocketDisconnect:\n        return\n",
      "showCopyButton": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "REQUEST AND EXPECTED RESPONSE\n",
      "size": 18,
      "color": "#2E7D32",
      "bold": true
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "text",
      "code": "Request: Connect ws://127.0.0.1:8000/ws; send \"hello\"\nResponse: The server sends `Echo: hello` back on the same connection.",
      "showCopyButton": false
    },
    {
